'''Plainfield''' is a town located in [[Washington County, Vermont]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,286.

== Geography ==
Plainfield is located at 44&amp;deg;16'41&quot; North, 72&amp;deg;25'37&quot; West.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 54.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (21.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  54.4 km&amp;sup2; (21.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.19% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,286 people, 487 households, and 317 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 23.6/km&amp;sup2; (61.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 520 housing units at an average density of 9.6/km&amp;sup2; (24.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 96.42% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.78% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.86% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.47% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.39% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.09% from two or more races.  1.40% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 487 households out of which 37.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 34.9% are non-families. 25.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.42 and the average family size is 2.93.

In the town the population is spread out with 23.7% under the age of 18, 12.9% from 18 to 24, 28.8% from 25 to 44, 24.4% from 45 to 64, and 10.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.1 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $38,750, and the median income for a family is $42,813. Males have a median income of $30,789 versus $29,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $17,980.  10.9% of the population and 7.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 9.2% of those under the age of 18 and 17.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Culture==
Although Plainfield is similar to many other rural [[New England]] towns by the numbers (size, population, etc.) it has a distinct flair which sets it apart from most surrounding communities.  [[Goddard College]] attracts a [[Liberal]], educated population that makes up a significant portion of the townspeople. Goddard graduates [[Phish]] have had a lasting influence on the cultural history of Plainfield as well. The town has two [[restaurants]], both high-quality and very casual, located in the village center neighboring each other (Southern [[BBQ]] and NY-style [[pizza]] respectively).  The [[village]] also has a community food [[co-op]], a modest [[art gallery]], and a used [[bookstore]] all within several hundred feet of each other.  Plainfield's atmosphere is distinct from popular [[tourist]] destinations in [[Vermont]] like [[Stowe, VT]] and [[Woodstock, VT]] in that its commercial activity is generated primarily from local residents.

