      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wilder''' is a [[census-designated place]] (CDP) and a [[village]] in the [[town]] of [[Hartford, Vermont|Hartford]], [[Windsor County, Vermont|Windsor County]], [[Vermont]]. It is home of the ''Wilder Dam'' located on the [[Connecticut River]]. Wilder is on the [[National Register of Historic Places|National Register]] as a Historic Village and is unique as an early planned community developed in part by Charles Wilder, owner of a local paper mill in the 1880's.

== Geography ==
Wilder is located at [[geographical coordinates]] 43° 40′ 22&quot; North, 72° 18′ 33&quot; West (43.672901, -72.309227). According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 2.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.22% is water.

