      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wachapreague''' is a town located in [[Accomack County, Virginia]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 236.

== History ==
Until 1872 this area was just a single farmhouse and its fields. Then a wharf was built and produce was shipped from here to northern markets. In 1884, a steamboat began making trips between Wachapreague and New York City. Hotel Wachapreague became a popular destination of visitors from the north. 

