      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Stuarts Draft''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Augusta County, Virginia]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 8,367.  Stuarts Draft was formerly known as the home of [[Shenandoah Acres]], a large manmade sand-bottom lake and beach, historically owned by the Blacka family, which closed in 2004.

== History ==
In 1749, Thomas Stuart purchased 353 acres near the [[South River (Virginia)|South River]], a tribuary of the [[South Fork Shenandoah River|South Fork of the Shenandoah River]].  'Draft' probably refers to the document drafting the land sale or is a reference to the river itself (draft is an old term for river or creek and is part of the name of several such in the area).  The plain on the south side of the river tends to channel the wind, thus forming a rather constant draft.

== Geography ==
[[Image:VAMap-doton-StuartsDraft.PNG|right|Location of Stuarts Draft, Virginia]]
Stuarts Draft is located at 38&amp;deg;1'39&quot; North, 79&amp;deg;1'44&quot; West (38.027515, -79.028760){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 51.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (19.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  51.4 km&amp;sup2; (19.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.05% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 8,367 people, 3,124 households, and 2,436 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 162.9/km&amp;sup2; (422.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,279 housing units at an average density of 63.8/km&amp;sup2; (165.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 95.27% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.44% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.26% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.20% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.05% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.29% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.49% from two or more races.  1.06% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 3,124 households out of which 38.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 62.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 22.0% are non-families. 18.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.66 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 27.0% under the age of 18, 7.7% from 18 to 24, 31.4% from 25 to 44, 23.0% from 45 to 64, and 10.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.0 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $45,342, and the median income for a family is $52,308. Males have a median income of $32,917 versus $26,414 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $18,463.  3.7% of the population and 2.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.7% of those under the age of 18 and 4.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

