== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 17,786 people, 5,663 households, and 3,884 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 554.7/km&amp;sup2; (1,436.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 5,892 housing units at an average density of 183.8/km&amp;sup2; (475.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 48.95% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 34.66% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.29% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 7.63% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.13% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.92% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 4.42% from two or more races.  9.74% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,663 households out of which 42.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 49.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 15.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 31.4% are non-families. 23.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 1.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.68 and the average family size is 3.21.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 25.2% under the age of 18, 8.4% from 18 to 24, 45.2% from 25 to 44, 18.6% from 45 to 64, and 2.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 125.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 133.6 males.

