There are 3,304 households out of which 28.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 39.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 42.7% are non-families. 33.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.62 and the average family size is 3.30.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 21.2% under the age of 18, 11.5% from 18 to 24, 41.6% from 25 to 44, 19.5% from 45 to 64, and 6.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 108.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 108.9 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $44,579, and the median income for a family is $43,211. Males have a median income of $31,444 versus $30,743 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $20,475.  18.7% of the population and 15.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 27.3% of those under the age of 18 and 17.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Notable locations ==
Seven Corners hosts several shopping centers that cater to [[Asian American|Asian]] and [[Hispanic]] residents from the [[Northern Virginia]] area, including [[Eden Center]] &amp;mdash; a &quot;[[Little Saigon]]&quot; composed almost entirely of Vietnamese-owned or -operated shops.

The [[parking garage]] of a [[Home Depot]] hardware store in Seven Corners was the scene of one of the shootings in the [[2002]] [[Beltway sniper attacks]]; Linda Franklin was slain while she returned to her car in the crowded parking garage.

